# Secure engineering contract

Authoritative guide (read before architecture or feature work):

`docs/security/CURSOR_SECURE_RUST_WEB_GUIDE.md`

## Non-negotiables

- Stack default: SvelteKit + TS, Rust + Axum, PostgreSQL, Docker; Redis only when justified.
- Security target: OWASP ASVS 5.0 Level 2 (+ selected L3 for admin/credentials/audit).
- Work in small phases; keep the app runnable after each phase.
- Before code changes: summarize what/files/security/tests.
- Never hard-code secrets; never expose stack traces/SQL/secrets to users.
- Never trust frontend validation; authorize every protected backend action (deny by default).
- No `unsafe` unless documented; no `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` on request paths.
- Do not invent schema/API fields — update contracts deliberately.
- Feature incomplete until: authz, validation, errors, logging, tests, docs.
- Prefer opaque HttpOnly Secure cookie sessions; Argon2id for passwords.
- Use SQLx bind params; explicit DTOs; idempotency for retried mutations.
- Fail closed on auth/config; pin deps; run fmt/clippy/test/audit gates.

## Bootstrap order

Follow guide Phase 0 → Phase 1 before product features (signup, CRM, SIMs, tickets).
